    "description": "feed-in-profile for onshore wind power plant nearly Erfurt (middle), Nordhausen (north), Gera (east) and Hildburghausen (swest); The feed-in profiles are based on weather data for a typical year from Meteonorm version 7.3.4.21143. Wind speed at a heigh of 10 meters is obtianed from the weather data and then scaled to the turbine hub height using the Hellman's exponent equation, as described in {1}. The adjusted wind speed is then used to calculate the power output based on the power curve of the Enercon E101 wind turbine, enabling the generation of realistic wind energy feed-in profiles for the locations. The data was collected in the ZO.RRO II project by Nordhausen University of Applied Science",
